{"notice_id": "16602081", "title": "Conservation Commission Public Hearing | Boston.gov", "cancelled": false, "public_testimony": true, "notice_url": "https://www.boston.gov/public-notices/16602081", "posted_at": "2026-07-28T11:34:00-04:00", "event_datetime": "2026-08-05T22:00:00Z", "address_1": "Virtual", "address_2": "", "page_text": "\n\n\n\n\n  Public Hearing\n\n\n\nNotice of Intent for DEP File No. 006-2134 and BOS File No. 2026-031 from Weston & Sampson Engineers, Inc., on behalf of the City of Boston Parks and Recreation Department for the proposed installation of a new arena at the Franklin Park Maintenance Yard, 275 Canterbury Street, Roxbury, MA (100ft Buffer Zone to BVW).\nNotice of Intent for DEP File No. 006-21XX from Foth Infrastructure & Environment, LLC, on behalf of the Massachusetts Port Authority for the proposed removal and replacement of concrete decking and repairs to underdeck spalling and concrete beams at Black Falcon Terminal, 88 Black Falcon Avenue, South Boston Waterfront, MA (LSCSF, DPA, 100ft Buffer to Coastal Bank).\n\nFranklin Park Maintenance Yard Park Ranger Paddock NOI\nCruiseport Deck & Beam Repair NOI\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  Regular Meeting\n\n\n\nRequest for a Certificate of Compliance for BOS File No. 2024-008 from the City of Boston Environment Department for restoration activities within the Mattahunt Woods property located in multiple parcels off of Itasca Street and Canaan Street, Mattapan, MA (IVW, 100ft Buffer to IVW).\nRequest for a Certificate of Compliance for DEP File No. 006-1762 and BOS File No. 2021-003 from the Massachusetts Department of Conservation and Recreation (DCR) for pool and parking lot renovations located at 75 & 95 Turtle Pond Parkway, Hyde Park, MA (Riverfront Area, Waterfront Area, 100ft Buffer to Inland Bank, 100ft Buffer to BVW, 100ft Buffer to IVW).\nRequest for a Certificate of Compliance for DEP File No. 006-2062 and BOS File No. 2025-027 from Childs Engineering on behalf of the Boston Planning & Development Agency for the demolition and replacement of approximately 61 deteriorated piles and associated timber wales and chocks under Pier 4, Eighth Street, Charlestown, MA  (Land Under Ocean).\nRequest for a Certificate of Compliance for DEP File No. 006-2123 and BOS File No. 2026-023 from Fort Point Associates, Inc., on behalf of Ocean Havens, LLC, for the rehabilitation of a degraded section of concrete deck at the Charlestown Marina, 1 Pier 8, 13th Street, Charlestown, MA (LSCSF).\nAdministrative Updates\nAcceptance of Meeting Minutes from July 1, 2026 and July 15, 2026\n \nThe Commission will hold a public meeting immediately following the last hearing or as appropriate following any hearing.  Plans and filings with the Commission may be requested via email from cc@boston.gov or viewed by appointment at the Environment Department, 26 Court Street, Floor 4, from 9 AM to 5 PM, Monday through Friday. Questions can be directed to cc@boston.gov or 617-635-3850.\n \n\n\n\n\n", "files": [{"file_label": "Official Filed Posting", "file_url": "https://www.boston.gov/sites/default/files/file/2026/07/08.05.2026%20Agenda%20-%20Conservation%20Commission.pdf", "download_success": true, "file_hash": "0845b6bf72b6afb8c38c0f370f707cd31891ad7fdedc6c3588399e71c6d30faf"}], "status": "ok", "checked_at": "2026-07-29T21:31:04.401102+00:00"}
