{"notice_id": "16492926", "title": "Boston Retirement Board Meeting | Boston.gov", "cancelled": false, "public_testimony": false, "notice_url": "https://www.boston.gov/public-notices/16492926", "posted_at": "2025-11-19T11:04:00-05:00", "event_datetime": "2026-10-21T13:00:00Z", "address_1": "Boston City Hall ", "address_2": "1 City Hall Square, Board Room, Room 816", "page_text": "\n\n\n\n\n  The standard administrative session agenda is as follows:\n\n\n\n\nConvene Meeting (Introduction of Members & Guests)\nAdministrative Session Minutes of previous board meeting\nOutstanding/Ongoing Administrative Issues\nOutstanding/Ongoing Investment Issues\nOutstanding/Ongoing Financial Issues\nOutstanding/Ongoing Operations Issues\nOutstanding/Ongoing Legal Issues\nAdjourn\nThe Board enters Executive Session in order to review applications for disability retirement benefits, accidental death benefits, member survivor allowance benefits, pension forfeiture, as well as litigation strategy.  At the conclusion of the Executive Session, the Board reconvenes in Administrative Session in order to consider the rest of the agenda items, if any, and adjourn.\n\n\n\n\n\n", "files": [{"file_label": "Official Filed Posting", "file_url": "https://www.boston.gov/sites/default/files/file/2025/11/Retirment%20For%202026_1.pdf", "download_success": true, "file_hash": "b75ee84e481db0befebdcfffa2bff88e6e003bc0cd64940ac24b3cc8acf68b08"}], "status": "ok", "checked_at": "2026-07-29T21:31:46.062261+00:00"}
